<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">01042026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>The United Arab Emirates has lobbied the US, Europe, and Asian navies for a UN Security Council resolution authorizing military force to reopen the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme> — and volunteered its own troops.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Abu Dhabi's move comes as Washington told allies to get their own oil, with Trump setting a two-to-three-week timeline to leave Iran and no plan to restore shipping through the waterway that carries a fifth of the world's crude.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>A Gulf state that's spent decades avoiding military exposure is now stepping into a vacuum the country that started this war created.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>American B-fifty-two strategic bombers have flown over Iranian airspace for the first time, with Defense Secretary Hegseth declaring air supremacy after the destruction of Iran's air defenses.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>The flights came the same week Trump told NBC the war is coming to an end — a contradiction that signals escalation, not withdrawal, to the eighty-eight million people living under those flight paths.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Hegseth's own words — that the point is to be unpredictable — suggest no strategy beyond coercion, and April sixth looms as the deadline for Hormuz negotiations that Iran says it hasn't joined.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Beijing has produced the war's first formal ceasefire framework.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Foreign Minister Wang Yi and Pakistan's Ishaq Dar proposed five points — immediate cessation of hostilities, protection of civilians and energy infrastructure, restored Hormuz passage, and a UN-based settlement process.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Qatar warned that Iran's Gulf strikes have crossed many red lines, but whether any party accepts a framework drafted by a power with its own strategic interests in the region remains the open question.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The Gran Grif gang massacred at least seventy people in Jean-Denis — the heart of Haiti's rice-growing Artibonite valley, where most of the country's food is produced.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>National police had withdrawn from the area, leaving self-defense units outgunned, and armed men are now pushing nineteen kilometres north toward Marchand Dessalines.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>This isn't just a killing — it's an assault on the food supply of eleven million people in a country the world has stopped watching.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Kataib Hezbollah seized freelance journalist Shelly Kittleson from central Baghdad — the first abduction of a Western reporter in Iraq in years.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>The FBI had warned Kittleson of credible threats four times in a single week before the Iran-aligned militia took her.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Iraqi security forces launched a manhunt and arrested one suspect, but Kittleson hasn't been found.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Security forces in Sudan arrested eleven university professors mid-strike as academics at thirty-five universities entered a third day of nationwide action.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>The professors' committee is demanding a revised salary structure, and organizers say a wider strike is being prepared across three cities.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>In a country consumed by civil war, the fact that universities are still functioning — and still resisting — is itself the story.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A leaked recording caught Hungary's foreign minister Szijjártó coordinating directly with Russia's Lavrov — promising to delist an oligarch's sister from EU sanctions and closing with the words, I am always at your disposal.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>She was removed from the sanctions list seven months later, confirming the promise was kept.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Orbán faces his toughest election in sixteen years on April twelfth, and the audio lands with the force of a verdict.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>FIFA's governance committee has dismissed a Palestinian complaint against Israeli football clubs based in illegal West Bank settlements, ruling the territory's legal status unresolved — setting aside fifty-nine years of UN resolutions that say otherwise.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>A separate complaint before the International Criminal Court now accuses FIFA's president of aiding war crimes through institutional cooperation with the occupation.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Normalization, it turns out, isn't passive — it requires active choices, and FIFA has made its choice clear.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>India's state oil companies hiked jet fuel prices a hundred and fifteen percent overnight — crossing two lakh rupees per kilolitre for the first time — while commercial LPG jumped nearly two hundred rupees per cylinder.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Airlines, for whom fuel is forty percent of operating costs, are already flying longer detour routes around West Asia that burn more of the fuel they now can't afford.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>A country that imports eighty-five percent of its oil through the Gulf is feeling the blockade in every kitchen and on every boarding pass.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's LNG suppliers have declared force majeure after the Hormuz war halted Qatar's exports, cutting twenty percent of global supply and idling four thousand five hundred megawatts of gas-fired generation.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Coal from South Africa and Indonesia is the only backup fuel, while the Iranian rial has quadrupled against the Pakistani rupee as border traders in Balochistan speculate on post-war appreciation.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Officials promised April electricity — a promise no one waiting in the dark believes.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>WTO ministerial talks in Yaoundé collapsed without extending the e-commerce moratorium — a twenty-seven-year exemption that shielded tech giants from digital customs duties.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Brazil blocked the US extension bid, and developing nations may now tax streaming, downloads, and cloud services for the first time in the history of the commercial internet.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Director-General Okonjo-Iweala is pursuing a side deal to restore the exemption, but the era of duty-free digital trade may already be over.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Nearly five thousand wildfire hotspots blanketed northern Thailand on Tuesday, pushing PM two-point-five to hazardous levels across Chiang Mai — a city that now tops global pollution rankings every spring.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Agricultural burns from three countries drive a seasonal haze no single government controls, and families with children are leaving for months at a time.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>A twenty twenty-three lawsuit demanding an emergency pollution plan remains unresolved — the courts move slower than the smoke.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A forty-year study at five-kilometre resolution has found that the Arabian Peninsula's wind resources rival Europe's best offshore sites, with the strongest corridors in central-western Saudi Arabia and the northern Red Sea.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>The finding arrives as the Hormuz closure turns Gulf oil infrastructure from an asset into a liability, stranding tankers and idling refineries.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Whether the region that built its wealth on fossil fuels will pivot to the resource blowing freely across its deserts is a question the war has made urgent.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers in Adelaide have found that microgravity cuts human sperm navigation by fifty percent — in simulated weightlessness, directional function collapsed entirely and mouse fertilization rates fell by a third.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>NASA's Artemis missions proceed to the Moon, but whether humans can reproduce beyond Earth has never been tested in actual space.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>The species' long-term future off-planet, God willing there is one, just got a serious asterisk.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A UK family lost access to every Google service — email, photos, Drive, years of their digital life — after their child's interaction with Gemini Live triggered a single moderation flag.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Google denied all appeals, and under current law it has no legal obligation to reverse the ban or even explain what the child said.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>One incident, one device, one child — and an entire family's digital existence erased without due process by a company that functions as infrastructure but answers to no one.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Thomson Reuters' CLEAR database — containing addresses, Social Security numbers, and ethnicity data — feeds directly into Palantir's system, which generates confidence scores that ICE uses to prioritize deportation raids.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>Reuters employees sent leadership a signed protest letter, but the data pipeline remains active and the contracts remain in place.</s> <break time="300ms"/> <s>The company most people know as a news wire is quietly one of America's largest surveillance data brokers — and the people in its database never consented to be scored.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>